  "content": {
    "blocks": [
      {
        "kind": "text",
        "body": {
          "en": "Functions describe mathematical relationships. IB SL requires understanding domain, range, inverse functions, composite functions, transformations, and key function families.",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "def",
        "label": {
          "en": "● Function concepts",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<p><strong>Domain:</strong> set of permitted inputs. <strong>Range:</strong> set of possible outputs. <strong>Composite:</strong> \\((f\\circ g)(x)=f(g(x)).\\) <strong>Inverse:</strong> \\(f^{-1}\\) exists iff \\(f\\) is one-to-one; \\(f(f^{-1}(x))=x.\\)</p><p>Graphically: \\(f^{-1}\\) is the reflection of \\(f\\) over \\(y=x.\\)</p>",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "thm",
        "label": {
          "en": "● Transformations of \\(y=f(x)\\)",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<table class=\"exam-table\" style=\"margin-top:6px\"><thead><tr><th>Transformation</th><th>Equation</th><th>Effect</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Vertical shift \\(+k\\)</td><td>\\(y=f(x)+k\\)</td><td>Up by \\(k\\)</td></tr><tr><td>Horizontal shift \\(+h\\)</td><td>\\(y=f(x-h)\\)</td><td>Right by \\(h\\)</td></tr><tr><td>Vertical stretch \\(a\\)</td><td>\\(y=af(x)\\)</td><td>Scale by \\(a\\) vertically</td></tr><tr><td>Horizontal stretch \\(\\frac{1}{b}\\)</td><td>\\(y=f(bx)\\)</td><td>Scale \\(x\\) by \\(1/b\\)</td></tr><tr><td>Reflect \\(x\\)-axis</td><td>\\(y=-f(x)\\)</td><td>Flip vertically</td></tr><tr><td>Reflect \\(y\\)-axis</td><td>\\(y=f(-x)\\)</td><td>Flip horizontally</td></tr></tbody></table>",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "def",
        "label": {
          "en": "● Key function families",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<table class=\"exam-table\" style=\"margin-top:6px\"><thead><tr><th>Family</th><th>Form</th><th>Key feature</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Linear</td><td>\\(f(x)=mx+c\\)</td><td>Constant rate of change</td></tr><tr><td>Quadratic</td><td>\\(f(x)=ax^2+bx+c\\)</td><td>Vertex, axis of symmetry</td></tr><tr><td>Exponential</td><td>\\(f(x)=ka^x+c\\)</td><td>HA at \\(y=c\\); multiplicative growth</td></tr><tr><td>Logarithmic</td><td>\\(f(x)=a\\log_b x+c\\)</td><td>VA at \\(x=0\\); inverse of exponential</td></tr><tr><td>Rational</td><td>\\(f(x)=\\frac{ax+b}{cx+d}\\)</td><td>VA and HA; one-to-one</td></tr><tr><td>Sinusoidal</td><td>\\(f(x)=a\\sin(bx+c)+d\\)</td><td>Amplitude \\(|a|\\), period \\(2\\pi/b\\)</td></tr></tbody></table>",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "explorer",
        "canvasId": "ibslTransCanvas",
        "title": {
          "en": "⊙ Explorer · Transformations of y = f(x)",
          "ar": null
        },
        "ariaLabel": {
          "en": "The base curve y equals x squared, in grey, and a transformed version y equals a times f of x minus h plus k, in blue",
          "ar": null
        },
        "dataPanel": {
          "btnId": "ibslTransDataBtn",
          "panelId": "ibslTransDataPanel",
          "descId": "ibslTransDataDesc",
          "rowsId": "ibslTransDataRows",
          "caption": {
            "en": "Sampled points on x² and its transformation",
            "ar": null
          },
          "columns": [
            {
              "en": "x",
              "ar": null
            },
            {
              "en": "x²",
              "ar": null
            },
            {
              "en": "g(x)",
              "ar": null
            }
          ]
        },
        "controls": [
          {
            "id": "ibslTransA",
            "label": {
              "en": "vertical stretch <b>a</b>: ",
              "ar": null
            },
            "min": -20,
            "max": 20,
            "value": 10,
            "step": 1,
            "valueDisplayId": "ibslTransAlab",
            "ariaLabel": {
              "en": "a",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "id": "ibslTransH",
            "label": {
              "en": "horizontal shift <b>h</b>: ",
              "ar": null
            },
            "min": -4,
            "max": 4,
            "value": 0,
            "step": 1,
            "valueDisplayId": "ibslTransHlab",
            "ariaLabel": {
              "en": "h",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "id": "ibslTransK",
            "label": {
              "en": "vertical shift <b>k</b>: ",
              "ar": null
            },
            "min": -4,
            "max": 4,
            "value": 0,
            "step": 1,
            "valueDisplayId": "ibslTransKlab",
            "ariaLabel": {
              "en": "k",
              "ar": null
            }
          }
        ],
        "readouts": [
          {
            "id": "ibslTransEq",
            "label": {
              "en": "y =",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": "1(x-0)² + 0",
            "colorClass": "indigo"
          }
        ],
        "note": {
          "en": "Grey is the base \\(f(x)=x^2\\); blue is \\(y=a\\,f(x-h)+k\\) — exactly the transformation table above, live.",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "workedExampleCard",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked Example 2.1",
          "ar": null
        },
        "problem": {
          "en": "\\(f(x)=2x+3,\\;g(x)=x^2-1.\\) Find \\((f\\circ g)(x)\\) and \\((g\\circ f)(x).\\)",
          "ar": null
        },
        "solution": {
          "en": "<p>\\((f\\circ g)(x)=f(x^2-1)=2(x^2-1)+3=2x^2+1.\\)</p><p>\\((g\\circ f)(x)=g(2x+3)=(2x+3)^2-1=4x^2+12x+8.\\)</p>",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "workedExampleCard",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked Example 2.2",
          "ar": null
        },
        "problem": {
          "en": "Find \\(f^{-1}(x)\\) for \\(f(x)=\\dfrac{2x-1}{x+3}.\\)",
          "ar": null
        },
        "solution": {
          "en": "<p>Let \\(y=\\dfrac{2x-1}{x+3}.\\) Rearrange: \\(y(x+3)=2x-1\\Rightarrow xy-2x=-1-3y\\Rightarrow x(y-2)=-3y-1.\\)</p><p>\\(f^{-1}(x)=\\dfrac{-3x-1}{x-2}=\\dfrac{3x+1}{2-x}.\\)</p>",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "cards",
        "items": [
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Composite functions",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( (f\\circ g)(x)=f(g(x)) \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Inverse functions",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( f^{-1}(f(x))=x \\); graph is reflection over \\( y=x \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "warn",
        "label": {
          "en": "Practice Problem",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<p>Let \\(f(x)=3x-1\\) and \\(g(x)=x^2+2.\\) Find \\(f^{-1}(x)\\) and solve \\((g\\circ f)(x)=14.\\)</p><details style=\"margin-top:8px\"><summary style=\"cursor:pointer;font-weight:600\">Show solution</summary><div style=\"margin-top:8px\"><p>\\(f^{-1}(x)=\\dfrac{x+1}{3}.\\)</p><p>\\((g\\circ f)(x)=(3x-1)^2+2=14\\Rightarrow(3x-1)^2=12\\Rightarrow 3x-1=\\pm2\\sqrt{3}.\\)</p><p>\\(x=\\dfrac{1\\pm2\\sqrt{3}}{3}.\\)</p></div></details>",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example-grid",
        "label": {
          "en": "Completing the square",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<p>Write \\(f(x)=2x^2-8x+5\\) in vertex form and state the vertex.</p><p><strong>Solution:</strong> \\(f(x) = 2(x^2-4x)+5 = 2(x-2)^2 - 8 + 5 = 2(x-2)^2 - 3\\)</p><p>Vertex: \\((2,-3)\\)</p>",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example-grid",
        "label": {
          "en": "Inverse function",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<p>Find \\(f^{-1}(x)\\) for \\(f(x) = \\dfrac{3x+1}{x-2},\\; x\\neq2\\).</p><p><strong>Solution:</strong> Let \\(y=\\dfrac{3x+1}{x-2}\\). Swap and solve: \\(x(y-3)=1+2y\\implies x=\\dfrac{2y+1}{y-3}\\).</p><p>So \\(f^{-1}(x)=\\dfrac{2x+1}{x-3},\\; x\\neq3\\).</p>",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "practiceProblem",
        "question": {
          "en": "<strong>Practice:</strong> The graph of \\(y=f(x)\\) passes through \\((1,4)\\). Write down the point on \\(y=f^{-1}(x)\\).",
          "ar": null
        },
        "solution": {
          "en": "By definition of inverse, \\((4,1)\\) lies on \\(y=f^{-1}(x)\\).",
          "ar": null
        }
      }
    ]
  }
}
